1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,077
T two D Compass helps researchers inspect public ClinicalTrials dot gov records for completed type two diabetes intervention studies.

2
00:00:06,077 --> 00:00:09,646
This narrated recorded-evidence walkthrough uses automated speech and captions.

3
00:00:09,646 --> 00:00:15,434
It combines dated browser evidence, exported tool results, real-model traces, and a new source-reference audit.

4
00:00:15,434 --> 00:00:20,747
The panels summarize those saved artifacts; this video is not a fresh screen recording or a new assistant run.

5
00:00:20,747 --> 00:00:27,084
Researchers repeatedly collect study identifiers, design, enrollment, interventions, registered outcomes, and results availability.

6
00:00:27,084 --> 00:00:32,457
Compass organizes the registry fields into a consistent evidence card, keeping source links and review flags attached.

7
00:00:32,457 --> 00:00:35,316
Its intended output is a starting point for human review.

8
00:00:35,316 --> 00:00:38,739
It does not turn registry descriptions into a treatment recommendation.

9
00:00:38,739 --> 00:00:43,816
The first tool searches for completed interventional studies with an explicit supported type two diabetes condition label.

10
00:00:43,816 --> 00:00:47,300
The second retrieves an evidence card for a specified trial identifier.

11
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:51,363
Both tools are read only and use a fixed public source, with no patient records.

12
00:00:51,363 --> 00:00:54,687
The browser and optional Databricks assistant use these same tools.

13
00:00:54,687 --> 00:00:59,515
The November twenty third signed-in browser review searched for MEDI zero three eight two, with a limit of three.

14
00:00:59,515 --> 00:01:04,093
The exported response reports live source mode, completed status, and interventional study type.

15
00:01:04,093 --> 00:01:07,016
The app also applied its explicit condition-label screen.

16
00:01:07,016 --> 00:01:11,545
The response is preserved so the visible summary can be checked against the actual returned JSON.

17
00:01:11,545 --> 00:01:16,458
The response returned these three study identifiers, each with its registry title and source URL.

18
00:01:16,458 --> 00:01:20,956
These are candidate records to inspect, not recommendations or a ranked evidence synthesis.

19
00:01:20,956 --> 00:01:25,584
A matching condition label also does not prove that every enrolled participant had type two diabetes.

20
00:01:25,584 --> 00:01:30,032
Population context and the complete registry record still need review before drawing conclusions.

21
00:01:30,032 --> 00:01:35,590
The same response reports three returned records, four examined records, and one excluded for its condition labels.

22
00:01:35,590 --> 00:01:38,803
It marks the search incomplete because the requested limit was reached.

23
00:01:38,803 --> 00:01:41,287
This is deliberately a bounded candidate search.

24
00:01:41,287 --> 00:01:44,271
Broadly labeled studies can be missed by the conservative screen.

25
00:01:44,271 --> 00:01:50,728
Users should therefore retain the coverage warning when exporting or explaining results, rather than presenting this list as an exhaustive literature search.

26
00:01:50,728 --> 00:01:53,956
The same review retrieved this specific study by its identifier.

27
00:01:53,956 --> 00:02:00,328
Its exported card reports a completed interventional study, a randomized parallel design, and enrollment of sixty five labeled actual.

28
00:02:00,328 --> 00:02:04,062
The card retains the notice, registry extraction pending human review.

29
00:02:04,062 --> 00:02:09,665
Enrollment also remains separate from the number analyzed for a particular outcome, which the current card does not determine.

30
00:02:09,665 --> 00:02:12,229
This record contains two primary outcomes.

31
00:02:12,229 --> 00:02:18,171
The example shown here is percent change in body weight to day fifty, paired with the reported timeframe, day one through day fifty.

32
00:02:18,171 --> 00:02:22,035
The full export also retains the glucose outcome and its timed sampling schedule.

33
00:02:22,035 --> 00:02:25,908
Compass keeps outcomes and timeframes together instead of reducing them to names alone.

34
00:02:25,908 --> 00:02:31,126
These are registry descriptions, not extracted numerical findings or proof of prospective specification.

35
00:02:31,126 --> 00:02:37,643
The export lets a reviewer trace enrollment back to the registry design module and enrollment count field, preserving the original value sixty five.

36
00:02:37,643 --> 00:02:42,221
It also retains the canonical study URL, retrieval timestamp, and registry update date.

37
00:02:42,221 --> 00:02:47,619
These dates answer different questions: when the app retrieved information, and when the registry record was updated.

38
00:02:47,619 --> 00:02:51,373
A second exported card is completed but has no results posted in the registry.

39
00:02:51,373 --> 00:02:53,092
Those are separate facts.

40
00:02:53,092 --> 00:02:59,404
Completed does not mean successful treatment, and no posted registry results does not prove that findings or publications are absent elsewhere.

41
00:02:59,404 --> 00:03:02,468
This study also has pediatric eligibility criteria.

42
00:03:02,468 --> 00:03:08,346
The complete eligibility text is retained as entry rules, not as observed characteristics of the actual enrolled participants.

43
00:03:08,346 --> 00:03:14,648
The reviewer used visible browser controls to export the search, three evidence cards, an error response, and assistant traces.

44
00:03:14,648 --> 00:03:18,137
Those files were downloaded and parsed during the November twenty third review.

45
00:03:18,137 --> 00:03:24,629
A reviewer can carry the source fields, review flags, and interpretation limits into a separate review rather than relying on a copied summary.

46
00:03:24,629 --> 00:03:29,187
The direct browser checks also retrieved an active study and retained its outside-completed-scope warning.

47
00:03:29,187 --> 00:03:32,576
A missing identifier returned not found without a substitute card.

48
00:03:32,576 --> 00:03:36,209
A no-match search returned zero candidates without claiming global absence.

49
00:03:36,209 --> 00:03:39,348
An invalid identifier triggered browser format validation.

50
00:03:39,348 --> 00:03:43,616
These are observed direct workflow behaviors, not four extra model-quality passes.

51
00:03:43,616 --> 00:03:47,899
The active exclusion record is separate from the ten-card source-reference accuracy denominator.

52
00:03:47,899 --> 00:03:51,572
The November twenty first model scenarios used frozen public snapshots.

53
00:03:51,572 --> 00:03:54,791
The November twenty third direct browser checks used the live registry.

54
00:03:54,791 --> 00:03:59,968
Frozen inputs make comparisons reproducible, while live retrieval separately tests current source access.

55
00:03:59,968 --> 00:04:04,097
The two modes can return different candidate sets, and neither should be relabeled as the other.

56
00:04:04,097 --> 00:04:10,089
Two current live cards also matched all twenty eight corresponding frozen reference groups, a limited two-card consistency check.

57
00:04:10,089 --> 00:04:15,272
This preserved October twenty eighth browser image illustrates the evidence-card layout for the same study identifier.

58
00:04:15,272 --> 00:04:22,505
Visible fields include completed status, results posted, actual enrollment, a review flag, a source link, and the export control.

59
00:04:22,505 --> 00:04:25,753
The image is historical evidence, not a new screen recording.

60
00:04:25,753 --> 00:04:31,801
The November twenty third exports just discussed are separate artifacts and provide the current direct browser observations and downloaded data.

61
00:04:31,801 --> 00:04:37,749
The saved automated suite passed two hundred ninety four tests, with no failures or errors, alongside static checks.

62
00:04:37,749 --> 00:04:42,617
Earlier package verification covered startup, browser assets, health, and both MCP tools.

63
00:04:42,617 --> 00:04:46,226
Actual local MCP replays also tested live and snapshot retrieval.

64
00:04:46,226 --> 00:04:50,614
These are software and integration checks, not two hundred ninety four clinical cases.

65
00:04:50,614 --> 00:04:55,832
Some tests use synthetic inputs or mocked model responses, so real-model evidence is reported separately.

66
00:04:55,832 --> 00:05:01,749
The delivered November twenty first archive contains twelve scenarios repeated twice, with all twenty four executions completing.

67
00:05:01,749 --> 00:05:04,738
The recorded model is Databricks G P T five five.

68
00:05:04,738 --> 00:05:09,466
The traces preserve fifty two model turns and thirty eight tool calls, all using snapshot data.

69
00:05:09,466 --> 00:05:14,940
Median case time was seventeen point five seconds, with a range of two point eight to thirty six point four seconds.

70
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:17,664
These timings are not hosted load-test results.

71
00:05:17,664 --> 00:05:24,571
The supplied review documents naming Chinelo and Mohammad report twelve of twelve scenario passes, including seven critical cases, in each run.

72
00:05:24,571 --> 00:05:29,174
Both injected upstream-failure scenarios visibly returned the controlled error and avoided invented evidence.

73
00:05:29,174 --> 00:05:32,882
These are reported team assessments, distinct from execution completion.

74
00:05:32,882 --> 00:05:40,774
Some document sign-off wording remains inconsistent and is disclosed in the evaluation report; raw trace review fields remain unchanged rather than being retrospectively overwritten.

75
00:05:40,774 --> 00:05:46,512
Two separate assistant passes extracted references from the saved source records and field contract before candidate cards were generated.

76
00:05:46,512 --> 00:05:54,124
After reconciliation, exact comparison matched all one hundred forty field groups across ten cards: eighty four development groups and fifty six held-out groups.

77
00:05:54,124 --> 00:05:56,633
Candidate and source hashes stayed unchanged.

78
00:05:56,633 --> 00:06:00,851
This completes an assistant source-reference audit, not independent human clinical approval.

79
00:06:00,851 --> 00:06:05,194
The original human approval gate remains pending, separate from the completed assistant audit.

80
00:06:05,194 --> 00:06:09,243
The signed-in direct browser workflow passed nine checks, including downloads.

81
00:06:09,243 --> 00:06:14,726
The initial two hosted assistant attempts failed at model authentication, with zero model turns and zero tool calls.

82
00:06:14,726 --> 00:06:16,465
Their traces are preserved.

83
00:06:16,465 --> 00:06:23,727
The hosted configuration differs from the November twenty first snapshot model, so those successful scenario runs do not by themselves prove the current hosted assistant.

84
00:06:23,727 --> 00:06:28,460
Any later successful run must be recorded and reviewed separately, rather than erasing these failures.

85
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:36,277
The public repository and delivery package let reviewers inspect the source, tool contracts, saved records, model traces, and evaluation results.

86
00:06:36,277 --> 00:06:44,839
The evidence now includes real snapshot model executions, supplied team scenario assessments, a completed assistant source-reference comparison, and current direct browser exports.

87
00:06:44,839 --> 00:06:48,092
Compass supports source-based human review of registry information.

88
00:06:48,092 --> 00:06:53,895
It does not rank treatments, prescribe care, replace a systematic review, or establish clinical effectiveness.

89
00:06:53,895 --> 00:06:56,479
Thank you for reviewing T two D Compass.